id: pm-by83yj
title: Core external-reference refusal recommends a flag absent from the CLI lexicon
description: "Current checkout create --stdin-json refuses an external_ref field as core_item_field_requires_dedicated_flag and recommends pm update <id> --external-ref <value>. Following that recovery fails because --external-ref is declared nowhere, including update. The refusal cannot supply its promised recovery."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T18:27:26.645Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T13:45:57.159Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#5628aec67334ad0f0d349bb7"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce in an isolated initialized tracker with unchanged-byte refusal evidence; align external-reference mutation support with public SDK contracts; generated help/contracts and actual dispatch agree; a negative control detects ghost recovery flags; all reserved-field recovery recommendations use declared executable paths
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-wg07
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: Every reserved-core-field refusal names an executable supported write path or truthfully states that no CLI mutation path is available.
actual_result: create --stdin-json advertises update --external-ref; following it exits 2 with a declared_nowhere unknown-option refusal.
