comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T18:27:26.645Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status corpus plus current exact external_ref/dedicated-flag search and open/in_progress inventories found no existing orphan external-reference recovery owner. Full public-surface parent metadata/history was read. Directly observed both refusal stages during GitHub intake. This issue stays open and unclaimed; current metadata-editor delivery does not claim the broader recovery contract fixed."
  "2026-10-12T09:52:30.253Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: remove synthesized reserved-field flags and route recovery from the real command registration contracts. external_ref has no dedicated create/update/close flag; preserve imported metadata compatibility and state that limitation truthfully instead of inventing a new transport mutation. Inventory every reserved core field so ghost flags cannot recur."
  "2026-10-12T10:16:50.698Z","harness:codex","All73 reserved core storage fields are now tested against executable create/update registrations. Direct CLI stdin create/update external_ref refusals preserve existing item+history bytes, emit no invented flag, and identify the missing dedicated mutation path. An isolated pre-fix-style synthesized --external-ref mutant fails the independent external_ref table row. Structured gate-strengthening evidence binds this regression and native transport checks; ordinary SDK imports/legacy stored references remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-12T10:54:38.138Z","harness:codex","Collection semantics are now single-sourced with structured item IO: dependencies/dep,comments/comment,type_options/typeOption and all other collection mappings come from one SDK-owned data table. Three independent collection-route assertions fail before this refinement and pass afterward; scalar routes and truthful unsupported external_ref refusal stay intact. The integration moved to tests/integration/sdk to preserve the unchanged120-file directory cap, with linked command replacement recorded through PM history."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:16:51.395Z","harness:codex",Storage field spelling is not a CLI mutation contract. Recovery must derive routes from executable registrations and state unavailable routes explicitly; create/update/close can have different support.
